  "goodToKnow": "Die Pressefreiheit is freedom of the press, guaranteed by Article 5 of the Grundgesetz, with the famous line Eine Zensur findet nicht statt (there shall be no censorship). The 1962 Spiegel-Affäre, when the government had the magazine's offices raided and editors arrested, became a landmark for press freedom in West Germany and led to the defence minister's resignation. It has no plural."
